# Host config: everything that differs between machines, in one file.
#
# The real file is ~/.config/minecraft/host.env, outside git.
# scripts/install.sh writes it, or copy this file there and edit it.
# Every key is optional: the units and start.sh fall back to the default
# shown for each key (today's Pi), so a missing host.env changes nothing.
#
# systemd reads it (EnvironmentFile=) only when a unit starts, so restart
# the units that use a key after changing it. Plain KEY=value lines only:
# no quotes, no spaces around "=", and no ~ or $VARS.
#
# Secrets don't go here; they go in secrets.env (see secrets.example.env).

# GitHub repo (owner/name) whose releases mc-agent installs. Read by
# mc-agent.service. Default: the repo whose CI built the running mc-agent,
# so a fork deploys its own releases.
#REPO=owner/name

# Your domain on Cloudflare. install.sh uses it to list the hostnames to
# set up. The pages still name their own domain for now.
#DOMAIN=example.com

# The Minecraft server folder: lazymc, start.sh and the worlds. Today this
# is the git checkout. Read by minecraft.service and play.service.
# Default: ~/minecraft_server
#SERVER_DIR=/home/you/minecraft_server

# Java heap for Paper: a number and M or G. Read by start.sh, which LazyMC
# runs under minecraft.service. install.sh picks about 60% of RAM.
# Default: 10G
#HEAP=10G

# Where each web app listens; Cloudflare Tunnel points at these. If you
# change one, change its health URL in deploy/release.json too. The static
# sites' addresses are in deploy/sites/<site>.env.
# Read by play.service and admin.service.
#PLAY_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8082
#ADMIN_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8081
